{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"assumptions_and_dependencies\":\"Canonical repositories are now resolved and pinned as vela-science/math@6fea63f2e7882fd9de0398868984cd88a17898f1, williamjblair/lean-proofs@accf62cb636c8909dd7e098e3f82b2140d3a192e, and the mounted Formal Conjectures@9cbe1d3c12998c786b7c2cd99ce28a21b6631f66.\",\"build_or_check_outcome\":\"Fetched exact shallow checkouts and ran fixed-string Git searches for every target selector and distinctive mathematical term. No covering duplicate was found in either canonical Math or lean-proofs; Formal Conjectures hits were confined to the stated target files and local related definitions. Source-page checks confirm #359’s prefix, #1052’s 87360 example, #1062’s [m+1,3m+2] construction, #835’s composite-case bound, and #14’s asymptotic question.\",\"case_id\":\"FIVE-01\",\"evidence\":\"Pinned repositories’ HEADs independently equal 6fea63f2e7882fd9de0398868984cd88a17898f1, accf62cb636c8909dd7e098e3f82b2140d3a192e, and 9cbe1d3c12998c786b7c2cd99ce28a21b6631f66. Exact duplicate queries returned no candidate-target matches in the first two repositories.\",\"limitations\":\"No prior Result Factory denominator list was encoded in the appendix, so searches cannot be claimed against unnamed denominators. Repository absence is bounded evidence, not novelty proof.\",\"proposed_result\":\"No case is presently classified duplicate. I am attempting independent Lean checks for the two executable proof candidates and the existing conditional bridge.\",\"question\":\"Aggregate independent evaluation for RESULTS-FIVE-01\",\"result_status\":\"dependency_finding\",\"result_type\":\"typed_non_result\",\"smallest_independent_check\":\"Run the same fixed-string searches at the three pinned commits; supply the omitted denominator locators for any required additional duplicate gate.\"}"}}
